    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d842-a1">

                <pb facs="0819" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg721"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">District attorney, ninth judicial
                            district of Louisiana, to the governor of
                            Louisiana.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tallulah, La.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The matter of the alleged lynching of
                    the Italians here was investigated by the grand jury which has just adjourned.
                    All the witnesses mentioned in your communication, whose attendance could be
                    compelled, were summoned and testified on oath that they knew nothing of the
                    affair. They, none of them, gave any testimony which implicated anyone, and
                    positively swore they knew nothing of the matter whatever.</p>
                <p>This is the third grand jury which has thoroughly investigated this matter, and
                    each investigation has been thorough and has resulted in failure to implicate
                    anyone.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. S. Holmes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
